      "content": "It's important to address severe diarrhea, especially if your child remains dehydrated and unresponsive or unwilling to wake up. While diluted apple juice can provide some hydration, I recommend calling your pediatrician first to get professional advice. If you notice any signs of severe dehydration (like dizziness, dry mouth, or lips, or extreme sunken eyes), then it's crucial to go to the ER immediately.",
